  "answer": "### Short Answer\nA VAT-registered exporter that sells 100% of its goods abroad can obtain a refund or tax credit for input VAT. This is provided under the provisions of the NIRC.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor VAT-registered exporters, this provision is beneficial as it allows them to recover the VAT they have paid on their inputs, effectively reducing their overall tax burden. To claim the refund or credit, the exporter must ensure compliance with the necessary documentation and filing requirements as stipulated by the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR). This includes maintaining proper records and submitting the appropriate claims within the prescribed periods.",
